  "notes": "Body split drawn from right-side photos (2023-07, 2025-03) and the left from behind (2023-05); the split's top end, where it meets the crown, is hidden by the wing in most shots (medium-low). 'BLUE MONSTER' and the small socks are drawn for the right side only: no photo used shows the lower left fuselage. Re-checked 2026-11-15: 'jetBlue' placed as on the standard (measured in metres on the A321neo N2017J and checked on A320s: x 0.174-0.356 of an A320, cap 1.57 m, lowercase 0.76 of the capitals); 'jetblue.com' on the A320's nacelle x 0.43-0.79 (read off N615JB and N627JB); the name under the cockpit given its length. The roundel moved aft to x 0.375 to sit just behind the title's end, as on the photos."
